-- The lease on a claimed reminder: the status and the timestamp.
--
-- Generated by drizzle-kit from the schema file, deliberately. Hand-writing
-- an enum value or a column that the schema file also declares leaves
-- drizzle's snapshot behind, and `drizzle-kit generate` then wants to add it
-- again for ever. Anything expressible in schema.ts belongs in a generated
-- migration; see 0004 for the parts that are not.
--
-- Why a lease exists at all: claiming used `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP
-- LOCKED` and then raised the attempt count, leaving the row `scheduled`.
-- SKIP LOCKED only holds for the life of the transaction, and the message is
-- sent *after* it commits -- so a second worker starting in the gap claimed
-- the same reminder and the customer was texted twice.
ALTER TYPE "public"."reminder_status" ADD VALUE 'sending' BEFORE 'sent';--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TABLE "reminders" ADD COLUMN "claimed_at" timestamp with time zone;